            <sparkle:version>17</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.7.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<!-- What Sparkle shows for 1.7.0. One file per version, English only. -->
<style>
  body { font: 13px -apple-system, sans-serif; color: #333; margin: 12px 16px; }
  h2 { font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 8px; }
  ul { padding-left: 20px; margin: 6px 0; }
  li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  p.quiet { color: #777; margin: 8px 0 0; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    body { color: #ddd; } p.quiet { color: #999; }
  }
</style>
<h2>Belay 1.7.0</h2>
<ul>
  <li><b>See what your agents are doing.</b> Working sessions now show small
      activity badges like shell, editing and search. Categories only, never
      your prompts or code.</li>
  <li><b>Background tasks keep the hold.</b> If agents or shell jobs keep
      running after a turn ends, Belay keeps your Mac awake and shows a
      background-task badge.</li>
  <li><b>Hooks clean up automatically.</b> Belay removes its entries when it
      quits and restores them on launch, so closed Belay never leaves agents
      pointing at a dead connection.</li>
  <li><b>Return summaries are more reliable.</b> Closing the lid no longer
      hides the while-you-were-away summary, and it now mentions if your Mac
      ran hot.</li>
</ul>
<p class="quiet">Also: dark wakes no longer look like stalls in diagnostics,
and sessions taking turns no longer flood the log.</p>]]></description>
