            <description><![CDATA[<!-- What Sparkle shows for 1.6.4. generate_appcast embeds any
     Belay-<version>.html beside the matching DMG, and publish-appcast.sh
     copies it there. One file per version, English only: Sparkle does not
     negotiate locale, and plain English is better than half-localised notes. -->
<style>
  body { font: 13px -apple-system, sans-serif; color: #333; margin: 12px 16px; }
  h2 { font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 8px; }
  ul { padding-left: 20px; margin: 6px 0; }
  li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  p.quiet { color: #777; margin: 8px 0 0; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    body { color: #ddd; } p.quiet { color: #999; }
  }
</style>
<h2>Belay 1.6.4</h2>
<ul>
  <li><b>Precise Detection reconnects itself.</b> If the connection to an
      agent breaks during sleep, Belay restores it when your Mac wakes.
      No relaunch needed.</li>
  <li><b>Long tool calls keep holding.</b> Rapid back-to-back activity no
      longer interrupts the hold during a long build or test run.</li>
  <li><b>One summary when you come back.</b> If Belay kept your Mac awake
      while you were away, it shows how long it held and how many runs
      finished. Statistics now also has a sortable list of recent sessions.</li>
  <li><b>A few rough edges are fixed.</b> Statistics no longer flicker on
      hover, and an Until time that has already passed no longer starts a
      timer for tomorrow.</li>
</ul>
<p class="quiet">Also: watched Cline sessions end when their files disappear,
old imported conversations no longer look active, and diagnostics stay fully
off when Local Reports is off.</p>]]></description>
